{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>From the river coming up, etc.</b> It should have said <b>seven cows coming up from the river</b>, for properly one should mention what is rising and afterward the place from which it rises. Or perhaps it intends to say that their entire coming-into-being was from the river, and therefore it put first that which brings them into being and afterward that which comes into being from it. And therefore, if it had said ״and behold seven cows coming up from the river,״ what would be heard is that the cows passed through the river and came up from it, but were not found in the river. Therefore it said ״from the river coming up seven cows״ — to say that from it they were found. And from this he sensed as well that he was dreaming a dream, as I explained in the verse ״and Pharaoh dreamed״ (Genesis 41:1). And the reason they showed him this vision was to convey that from the river itself the two likenesses would come into being — and this is what Yoseph interpreted, that they are seven years of plenty and seven years of famine, and both of them come into being from the river itself, whether it rises or does not rise; and therefore he saw in the dream that the cows' coming-into-being was from the river."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:24.009354802Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}